        }
      ],
      "updated": 1782746792621,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Adjacent cell of (1,2) :\n(cx + 1, cy) and (cx, cy + 1) = (2, 2) and (1, 3)\n\nAdjacent cell of (2,3) :\n(cx, cy - 1) and (cx -1 , cy) = (2, 2) and (1, 3)\n\nThe comparison between (vx - 1, vy - 1) and (cx, cy + 1) determines whether the Nord (N) branch of the vertex exists.\nThe comparison between (vx - 1, vy - 1) and (cx, cy + 1) determines whether the west (W) branch of the vertex exists.\n\nThe comparison between (vx, vy) and (cx, cy - 1) determines whether the east (E) branch of the vertex exists.\nThe comparison between (vx, vy) and (cx - 1, cy) determines whether the south (S) branch of the vertex exists. ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Adjacent cell of (1,2) :\n(cx + 1, cy) and (cx, cy + 1) = (2, 2) and (1, 3)\n\nAdjacent cell of (2,3) :\n(cx, cy - 1) and (cx -1 , cy) = (2, 2) and (1, 3)\n\nThe comparison between (vx - 1, vy - 1) and (cx, cy + 1) determines whether the Nord (N) branch of the vertex exists.\nThe comparison between (vx - 1, vy - 1) and (cx, cy + 1) determines whether the west (W) branch of the vertex exists.\n\nThe comparison between (vx, vy) and (cx, cy - 1) determines whether the east (E) branch of the vertex exists.\nThe comparison between (vx, vy) and (cx - 1, cy) determines whether the south (S) branch of the vertex exists. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
